{
  "id": "ss.proj.vine-snare",
  "name": "Snare",
  "description": "What a held body is wearing: two turns of the vine's own cord round its feet, with the tail still trailing off where the rest of the plant is. Drawn as one continuous wind rather than as two rings, because a ring is a hoop something is standing inside and a wind is a thing tied on \u2014 the second turn sits a little high and a little left of the first, which is what a cord does when it is pulled tight round something.\n\nIt exists because the hold needed to be legible on the body rather than only on the plant. A green wash says *something* is wrong with that animal; a cord round its feet says what. The palette is the vine's exactly \u2014 `$moss.dark2` with a `$moss` lit edge and `$blood.dark2` barbs \u2014 so the two read as one object at a glance, which is the whole job. Flattened to 0.52 and laid under the body it belongs to; `meta.radius` is the wind's own reach so the game can size it off whatever it is tied to.",
